From: Albrecht Lohofener <albrechtloh@gmx.de>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: smi: lower bound for the SMI clock delay

On the Raspberry Pi Zero with the 4-port managed switch HAT, SMI transfers
to the RTL8367S fail at random. The same probe stops at a different
register each time:

  rtl8365mb-smi switch: ACK timeout
  rtl8365mb-smi switch: failed to read chip id and version: -ETIMEDOUT

and, on a later bind,

  rtl8365mb-smi switch: found an RTL8367S switch
  rtl8365mb-smi switch: ACK timeout
  rtl8365mb-smi switch: failed to probe SerDes chip option: -ETIMEDOUT

The variants ask for clk_delay = 10 ns between edges of the bit-banged
MDC/MDIO lines. On the Pi's GPIOs that is practically no delay at all: the
clock runs as fast as the CPU can toggle the pins, and MDIO is sampled
before the switch had time to drive it.

Delay at least smi_clk_delay_ns (default 5000 ns) instead. Measured on
the hardware: at 10 and 1000 ns the probe fails every time, at 5000 ns it
succeeds, the switch registers and lan1-lan4 come up. Internal pull-ups on
MDC/MDIO (gpio=17,27=pu) made no difference. The SMI clock drops to about
100 kHz. The parameter is writable in /sys/module/realtek_dsa/parameters/,
so other values can be tried with an unbind/bind without a new kernel.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [workaround, the real limit is board specific]
Signed-off-by: Albrecht Lohofener <albrechtloh@gmx.de>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/realtek-smi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/realtek-smi.c
@@ -44,9 +44,20 @@
 
 #define REALTEK_SMI_ACK_RETRY_COUNT		5
 
+/*
+ * Lower bound for the time between two edges on the bit-banged SMI lines.
+ * The variants ask for 10 ns, which on a fast CPU with fast GPIOs (Raspberry
+ * Pi) leaves no time for the switch to drive MDIO before it is sampled, and
+ * transfers fail at random with "ACK timeout".
+ */
+static unsigned int smi_clk_delay_ns = 5000;
+module_param(smi_clk_delay_ns, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(smi_clk_delay_ns,
+		 "Minimum delay between SMI clock edges in ns (default 5000)");
+
 static inline void realtek_smi_clk_delay(struct realtek_priv *priv)
 {
-	ndelay(priv->variant->clk_delay);
+	ndelay(max(priv->variant->clk_delay, smi_clk_delay_ns));
 }
 
 static void realtek_smi_start(struct realtek_priv *priv)
